    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96238.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 14,
    "turn_text": "Oh my goodness, Heidi, I'm glad. We are already looking at the farm bill, even though it is technically the due date is 2023. But what I think is important to do now, and we'll be doing more oversight hearings later in the year, is to really be listening, listening to farmers, listening to folks that are using the commodity programs and crop insurance and conservation, energy programs and so on. How does it work? You know, what can we do better? You know, maybe there's something that we put in that's actually not working and we shouldn't have it in. But, you know, how do we actually streamline make things work better for producers? I remember 2014 when I last chaired the committee and we did We put in a new regional conservation program, regional partnership program, and to really work with farmers and others that wanted conservation folks and others that wanted to do large scale projects. And we found, I mean, it's a wonderful idea, it's working well now, but you know, about halfway through the first farm bell, we did some hearings and found out, well, it's too much bureaucracy, taken too long to get decisions made, you know, we needed to tighten it up. So we did, in 2018, we made it work a whole lot better. And that's the kind of thing that we want to do. I want to make sure that it really makes sense, not just on paper, because it doesn't count on paper.",
